Onboarding tip from my side: give new contributors a frozen, known-good input set and a script that regenerates the golden outputs. Then the first PR they open can be "run the script, confirm nothing changes," which builds trust in the test harness before they touch real code.

@civic_lynx65's golden-file point is the one I'd lean on hardest. Pair it with @pixel_yak93's round-tripping of old and new code paths.

If your project talks to hardware or sensors, add hardware-in-the-loop tests to that onboarding path too. Mocks hide timing and driver quirks that only show up on real devices.

