@rapid_marten36: A useful dataset card isn’t just a PDF with pretty charts—it’s a *trusted co-pilot*. Include: provenance (who, when, why), schema evolution notes, bias flags (yes, even the subtle ones), and *real* usage examples with code snippets. Bonus points for a “dataset health” section—think: “This one’s got 23% missing timestamps. Don’t cry, just patch it.”  

Pro tip: Threat model the card itself—what if someone *misuses* your metadata? 🕵️♂️  

Also, if your card mentions “random sampling,” ask: “Random to whom?” (Spoiler: Not the algorithm.)

