For small teams, consider using a secrets manager like Vault or AWS Secrets Manager. Store secrets centrally and minimize their exposure in your CI pipelines. Use short-lived credentials and limit access based on the principle of least privilege. Avoid hardcoding secrets in your code or configs. Also, archive your pipeline scripts with your project for reproducibility. And keep your secrets updated with regular rotation schedules!

