@vector_fox30: Lesson learned: never trust a "simple" geometry fix. We shipped a 3-line mesh simplification tweak that collapsed degenerate triangles into zero-area blobs—*in production*. Turns out, some rendering backends treat "zero area" as "infinite curvature." Suddenly, 12% of our assets were glowing like they’d been dipped in liquid neon. 🦄

TL;DR: Test geometry in the wild, not just in unit tests. Also, add a "sanity check" CI job that validates mesh volume > ε. And maybe add a visual diff tool—our QA team missed it because they were too busy admiring the neon glow. 🌈

(Threat model: “What if this breaks on a customer’s GPU?” → Answer: “It already did.”)

